WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.840
In the previous videos, you've seen us buying this
 big piece of land and working on it.

00:00:04.051 --> 00:00:07.562
We spend a lot of time building,
renovating and clearing the land.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.600
But, there's one thing we never mentioned,
and it's probably the most risky thing we ever did.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.209
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.680
So, about two years ago,
we bought this big piece of land.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:19.969
It's around ten hectares.

00:00:19.969 --> 00:00:23.691
And, by far the scariest thing,
when we were buying this piece of land...

00:00:24.143 --> 00:00:26.252
We bought it with a hole in the middle.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.220
Let me explain.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.067
See, this is the map of the land, and this is our land.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:33.171
This big circle in the middle is not ours.

00:00:33.171 --> 00:00:36.440
And, this circle is actually pretty big, with one hectare.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.960
It's very close to Basekamp.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.880
So, here we have Basekamp, and the workspace.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.520
Here is the road,
and already here is the neighboring land.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.960
So, all around here are the edges.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.080
You can see it marked very well with the poles.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.407
This is quite scary!

00:00:53.407 --> 00:00:57.600
Buying a land that close by a neighboring land,
and really all surrounded with it.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.960
Because, maybe the neighbor decided to start living here...

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.720
So, then they have to drive to Project Kamp every day,
 which is kind of awkward.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:09.680
Maybe, they start a stinky chicken farm,
so it would smell here all the time!

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.040
Or maybe, they decide to build a noisy factory...

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:16.200
It would really be in the middle,
like in the heart of Project Kamp.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:21.320
So, it seemed like a very stupid thing,
to buy your land like that...

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.960
Not owning the middle land...

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.560
But, so far, it's actually growing quite 'well'.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.688
So, after a year or something, when we came here...

00:01:32.688 --> 00:01:35.818
We met the neighbor,
and we also found as well on his land.

00:01:35.818 --> 00:01:39.240
And, we asked him:
''Could we use that for water on our land?''

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.400
And he said: "Yeah! Sure!''

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.866
Which was a good point, that we started meeting each other.

00:01:44.866 --> 00:01:50.320
We saw they're quite friendly, and nice people,
that are happy that we're here.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.080
I think that's kind of how we bought this land.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.800
Just hoping that the neighbor would be okay!

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:59.560
I would say it's been very risky, because you never know 
what neighbor you're going to end up with...

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.240
And, you have a lot of doom scenarios out there,
 of people fighting with their neighbor...

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:09.840
Bu,t I think, deep down inside, we fully trusted on hoping
people would find our way out of this.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.520
So, now, we made an agreement that was the next step
 that we would actually buy the land, which is cool!

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.012
Still haven't officially bought it, 
but I guess we both agreed!

00:02:19.012 --> 00:02:20.120
We trust each other!

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:26.160
So, now we can start using the land,
but we actually haven't really properly seen it yet.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.160
So, as a first step, we're going to discover it with a drone.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.600
We are here and the neighboring land is here.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.680
It's really in the middle of our land.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.694
If you have a closer look,
it seems like some really cool things are there!

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.923
Like some ruins on the land...

00:02:46.923 --> 00:02:49.040
Looks pretty cool from above!

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.720
And, some other hidden structures covered in bushes here...

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.440
Not sure what those are.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.440
Some sort of a small ruin or tiny brick house...

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.000
And, with it, seems another granite ruin next to it.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:05.680
Overall, it looks like it has a lot of spiky bushes and vegetation, 
green areas and full of brambles.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.720
So, yeah, that's all we can see for now with the drone.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.360
Let's have a look on the ground and explore those structures! 

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:15.360
I'm curious to see what they look like from close by!

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.240
So, here's the border.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.240
We're going to have a look what's there.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.320
A lot of mimosas around here.

00:03:44.497 --> 00:03:46.229
A little open field.

00:03:46.229 --> 00:03:48.208
Here's the well!

00:03:48.931 --> 00:03:55.160
The neighbors always talked about the overflow
 of our well should be somewhere here...

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.956
It's a bit wet on the bottom...

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.757
Yuck!

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.760
Wet socks!

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.760
This is the overflow of our well that we use.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:31.720
And, as you can see, 
the water is still flowing into the reservoir there.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:35.560
Almost empty, but it's still wet in here.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.400
Okay, first up, the well overflow and water reservoir.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:28.760
A big open, grass field with a lot of brambles.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.040
This is how I made my way to the field.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.360
A big eucalyptus tree, and a pine tree.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.800
Some ruin there?

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.240
Lots of spiky bushes!

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:10.777
I climbed up to the stone ruin...

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.718
Cool old ruin!

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:24.456
Something burned there...

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.547
It looks a bit collapsed.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.640
Many more native trees around here!

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:35.640
Less mimosas, which is good.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.800
Some roof tiles?

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.200
Another sort of ruin.

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:26.560
Now, we are here under the trees.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:53.240
Big old pine trees!

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:00.293
Another ruin?

00:08:01.829 --> 00:08:03.466
It looks very low.

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:09.307
Hard to access...

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:15.120
That's the border with our land, with the poles.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:18.120
This is really right at the edge!

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:27.960
Another big old pine tree with actual pine cones.

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:29.880
It's a shame it burned down...

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.640
It must have been nice to have this big tree.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:35.840
Not anymore...

00:08:38.219 --> 00:08:41.115
Here, I found the burned pine tree.

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:54.320
Making my way back to the ruin...

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:02.760
And, back on the big field.

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:04.676
I'm going to see that side.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:38.760
Here's some sort of a weird, dead, big, open field?

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.977
With a lot of eucalyptus, actually.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.000
And, pine!

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:51.160
Here's the path I travelled to the weird eucalyptus field.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:08.277
A grass patch.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:10.915
Random...

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:18.120
It's quite a big height difference here.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:19.795
Kind of cool!

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.967
Another little grass patch...

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:35.635
With many nice flowering bushes.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.417
This is the location of the smaller field.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:42.357
It's very peaceful here!

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:08.400
Okay, back to our land here.

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.396
We are back in the big field.

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:39.565
A cool big rock!

00:11:44.984 --> 00:11:47.984
Another burnt tree...

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:15.120
So, here is the big rock.

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:17.120
And there, you can see the big rock from our land!

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:19.280
Cool!

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.134
Here's our big grass patch.

00:12:21.917 --> 00:12:23.996
It's some cool land!

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.060
And, here is the big rock.

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:28.960
Nice adventure exploring this hectare!

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:31.960
I hope you got a rough idea of this place!

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:36.960
So, today we're going to brush cut on the land.

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:39.997
We're going to clean up the bushes,
 and the vegetation.

00:12:39.997 --> 00:12:45.103
To see what's underneath all of the rocks, the ruins, the well...

00:12:45.103 --> 00:12:46.640
I'm kind of curious to see what's all there!

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:49.920
So, it's time to chop some bushes!

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:20.240
So, here we are, in the open space of the land.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:23.560
I think there's a wall all the way there, but I'm not sure...

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:25.831
So, I thought:
''Maybe I'll start with that one.''

00:13:25.831 --> 00:13:28.397
To open it up, and to see what's underneath.

00:13:28.397 --> 00:13:29.640
A lot of brambles on top...

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:32.520
So, this could already take me a day,
 to just brush cut it...

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:01.720
So, this oak tree was fully covered with brambles.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.610
Now, it fell down and because of the weight...

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:05.592
It couldn't hold itself.

00:15:05.592 --> 00:15:09.000
So, now, we're going to put up a rope,
to make sure it's up again and so it can grow.

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:13.440
I got an old mimosa and a hammer.

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:19.297
We're going to give it some extra support,
 so it can stand up and become a big old tree!

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.800
The wall is now cleared up!

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:53.240
It's still quite rough, with sand and brambles and stuff...

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:54.256
But, that's for later!

00:15:54.256 --> 00:15:56.240
At least, we can now see what is actually there.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:57.593
It's pretty cool!

00:15:57.593 --> 00:15:59.520
It's nice to have a terrace is on the land!

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:01.600
Here, you can see the chopped field from above.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.680
Here's the wall that makes it a terrace.

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:07.320
It was probably used to grow vegetables,
and this is the oak tree.

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:08.680
I hope it will survive...

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:17.480
This is the sound of defeating spiky bushes.

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:27.717
Sounds good, when they're all dry and squeezed.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:34.720
So, here's the area we just chopped, and I realized actually 
that the well should just be here...

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:37.680
A lot of vegetation there.

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.680
But, I think it's very green,
because there's a lot of water there.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:45.384
I think I am going to chop here,
and see if we can find that well.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.040
So, it looks like it's here!

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:24.255
Let me show you!

00:17:24.255 --> 00:17:26.040
Some little stairs there!

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:29.400
Here's a basin in the overflow from the well.

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:31.938
And then, there is the pathway.

00:17:32.661 --> 00:17:36.934
I think it's cleaning up some more, to see what's all there!

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:43.240
It's now cleaned up!

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:45.280
Let me show you some things we found.

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:47.880
A pretty cool old wall here!

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:51.160
The overflow from the well,
with the water coming out here.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:54.320
It's bit covered with stuff...

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:57.320
Here's some old steps they made from stones.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:59.000
I think there is the regulator.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:00.397
Not sure what for...

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:04.240
And then, the water flows here...

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:07.400
It gets more wet, and there's a big basin.

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:11.945
Where the water stays.

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:15.030
It looks pretty cool!

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:17.560
So, here's the chopped road through the spiky bushes.

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:20.560
There you can see the basin of the well overflow.

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:23.960
So, next, we're going to do this grass patch in the middle.

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:27.040
Because, the grass is getting pretty high,
and some brambles start to grow.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:29.840
We're going to chop this all smooth.

00:19:29.840 --> 00:19:31.480
Then, we go to the ruin.

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:11.000
So, the field is now all chopped,
and now we're going to continue there to the ruin.

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:12.645
The last part!

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.255
So, here it is!

00:20:38.255 --> 00:20:40.920
A big rock in front, some roses...

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:44.367
They need a bit help here!

00:21:27.960 --> 00:21:33.440
Everything is now cleaned up around the ruin.

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:36.160
Now, we can have a look and explore a little bit!

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:39.240
We can have a fully walk around the ruin here.

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:43.240
Some nice big old granite rocks!

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:49.288
Over here, I wanted to chop it, but it all 
had these blossoming roses, so I could not.

00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:50.570
I could not...

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:51.733
Maybe later.

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:58.080
I think it used to be the hinge of the door...

00:21:59.720 --> 00:22:02.720
A lot of tiles on the floor...

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:06.040
Probably because the fire burned the wooden beams,
 with the roof tiles on top.

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:09.440
So, the wood is gone,
and the roof tiles are here.

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:13.640
It seems like it was a double floor.

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:16.000
Some metal chains?

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:18.036
I don't know what happened there.

00:22:23.274 --> 00:22:27.202
Some traces from the fire, with some molten aluminum?

00:22:30.400 --> 00:22:33.880
Jars and glass...

00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:42.720
It's like the ruin itself is built on 
this big granite stone right here.

00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:47.800
Yes, this is some of the burnt roof.

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:50.847
Another plate to eat on...

00:22:50.847 --> 00:22:53.305
Some metal door lock...

00:22:54.360 --> 00:22:55.861
Another thing...

00:22:58.520 --> 00:23:04.320
Up here, we have a molten rain coat or something hanging?

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:11.280
Yeah, something molten...

00:23:11.280 --> 00:23:12.100
Fabric.

00:23:12.642 --> 00:23:14.280
Over here is a big, cool, flat rock.

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:20.280
One of the neighbors actually told us,
that they used to dry their corn here on this flat rock.

00:23:20.440 --> 00:23:22.746
Maybe this was also some sort of storage?

00:23:23.830 --> 00:23:24.952
So, yeah, that's the ruin!

00:23:24.952 --> 00:23:27.150
A pretty nice location with the big rock outside!

00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:29.407
It seems like a fun project to renovate.

00:23:36.400 --> 00:23:40.080
So, finally, we're going to have a look at the two ruins there.

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:42.560
Those are also the ones I didn't really see properly yet...

00:23:42.560 --> 00:23:44.680
Because, the rest was a bit more accessible.

00:23:44.680 --> 00:23:46.560
But, this is really dense...

00:23:46.560 --> 00:23:48.280
It's a lot of vegetation here.

00:23:48.280 --> 00:23:49.200
Let me show you actually.

00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:55.160
So, yeah, and somewhere there, or there...

00:23:56.160 --> 00:23:57.982
I'm not sure.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:05.880
So, we're just going to start chopping the pathway,
and hopefully we'll find it!

00:25:34.920 --> 00:25:35.960
Sorry!

00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:53.000
So, let me show you what we found here in this ruin.

00:25:54.040 --> 00:26:00.480
It's also built on a big granite rock, 
and the ruin itself is in a bit rougher condition...

00:26:00.480 --> 00:26:03.480
It's more like clay and smaller stones.

00:26:04.640 --> 00:26:06.800
Looks like there was a small window there.

00:26:06.800 --> 00:26:09.520
There's another one there, like a door.

00:26:09.520 --> 00:26:12.520
So, it looks like there was a double floor.

00:26:13.200 --> 00:26:15.086
If we go out...

00:26:17.520 --> 00:26:20.720
There's another little room here,
and it's very low.

00:26:20.720 --> 00:26:23.800
I'm not sure, if there's just a lot of stuff here,
 like roof tiles and stones.

00:26:24.400 --> 00:26:27.400
Well, it was just a little room.

00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:32.640
Small room.

00:26:32.640 --> 00:26:35.640
Bigger room!

00:26:38.360 --> 00:26:41.120
So, this is one sort of ruin.

00:26:41.120 --> 00:26:47.640
And then, here's the other building from bricks, 
and it has three of these small rooms.

00:26:49.080 --> 00:26:51.360
Three cool rooms! 

00:26:51.360 --> 00:26:53.326
They could be three bedrooms.

00:26:54.290 --> 00:26:58.309
As you can see, it was also built on granite, 
so maybe it was an older ruin before...

00:26:58.309 --> 00:27:03.010
They put bricks on top, what they often do here.

00:27:03.720 --> 00:27:06.720
Also here, you can see the granite.

00:27:06.840 --> 00:27:10.217
Yeah, these look like three pretty cool places!

00:27:11.150 --> 00:27:15.440
So, that was everything to be found on the land for now!

00:27:15.520 --> 00:27:17.436
Wow! A big crack there!

00:27:19.240 --> 00:27:20.760
Anyways...

00:27:21.720 --> 00:27:24.720
I don't know what comes after this!

00:27:25.440 --> 00:27:27.640
So, those were the last two ruins on the land.

00:27:27.640 --> 00:27:28.600
Well, I think...

00:27:28.600 --> 00:27:29.783
That's all we could find!

00:27:29.783 --> 00:27:31.520
It's still quite hidden from above.

00:27:31.720 --> 00:27:34.720
But, you can actually access it pretty well from the bottom!

00:27:36.120 --> 00:27:37.936
That's all on the middle land

00:27:37.936 --> 00:27:43.560
We have the wall, the grass patch, the well, 
granite ruin, brick ruin and another ruin.

00:27:44.000 --> 00:27:46.378
Still more to explore,
but for now we know enough.

00:27:47.101 --> 00:27:49.301
So, that's kind of the story of the middle land!

00:27:49.301 --> 00:27:52.560
And, up until now, we still didn't officially buy it.

00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:56.040
But, we're just going to continue to take it into our plans.

00:27:56.040 --> 00:27:59.240
Because, we have trust and faith,
that we will work it out with the neighbor.

00:28:00.240 --> 00:28:04.360
This is actually going to be quite an essential land
 for Project Kamp, because it's really the center!

00:28:04.560 --> 00:28:09.005
So, the long term plan would be that we 
move the living situation to this land more.

00:28:09.005 --> 00:28:12.480
And, the current Basekamp will become more of a workspace area.

00:28:12.920 --> 00:28:15.920
You actually can see more of these plans in the research module!

00:28:16.840 --> 00:28:23.040
And, for now, the first next step is we're going 
to make an access area, so that we can bring a pig trailer here.

00:28:23.160 --> 00:28:27.840
We're going to build our first Level 2 house, 
and that's actually going to be the next video!

00:28:27.840 --> 00:28:31.040
If you already want to see that,
make sure to support this on Patreon!

00:28:31.480 --> 00:28:34.520
Or not, and subscribe,
and you will see it popping up on YouTube.

00:28:34.960 --> 00:28:36.861
Thanks for watching!
See you in the next video!

